  "license": "GPL-3.0-or-later",
  "comparison": "Complete finite, single pole, double pole: abs(value-reference)/max(1,abs(reference)) <= 1e-9 for DP and MP. The original Ninja rational split is also asserted for DP; MP records its basis-dependent difference.",
  "commands": [
    "CARGO_TARGET_DIR=\"$PWD/.ninjars-build/cargo\" python3 vendor/ninjars/tests/replay.py --precision dp --output docs/benchmarkfolder/data/bridge-dp-replays.json",
    "CARGO_TARGET_DIR=\"$PWD/.ninjars-build/cargo\" python3 vendor/ninjars/tests/replay.py --precision mp --output docs/benchmarkfolder/data/bridge-mp-replays.json"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "MP fixture replay promotes the archived binary64 input numbers; genuine binary128 transport is separately tested using 1+2^-100 in smoke.f90 and the Rust unit suite.",
    "MP uses one process-wide Symbolica worker with independent context states. Under a restricted Symbolica license, no other Symbolica process may be active for this user.",
    "Generic CC/rational split convention is documented at pinned upstream crates/ninjars-cli/README.md and crates/ninjars-symbolica/tests/fast_parity.rs; MadLoop uses complete Laurent coefficients and discards this diagnostic."
  ],
